  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRRS DRC 2025 &#x2013; UNICEF IMO</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The surge deployment of a water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH) Cluster Information Management Officer (IMO) in Goma, Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC), is essential due to the escalating humanitarian crisis caused by the latest resurgence of conflict involving the M23 armed group in the East. This renewed violence has led to massive displacement, with thousands of people fleeing Internally Displaced Persons (IDP) sites, seeking secondary displacement solutions in collective sites or attempting to return to areas destroyed by past conflict events. The lack of access to WASH services and infrastructure has increased the risk of cholera. Effective information management is critical to ensure that the response is data-driven, well-coordinated, and responsive to the urgent needs of affected communities.</narrative>
  </description>
